    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project has just the one concrete test class, `AcceptanceTest`, with 2 tests; `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper). Both new acceptance tests pass and nothing regressed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date behavior for `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this field is now on both the request DTO (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and the response DTO (`OwnerDto`), generating a `java.time.LocalDate` that Jackson serializes as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the `registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` column, with a getter/setter and a small `@PrePersist` callback (`defaultRegistrationDate`) that fills in `LocalDate.now()` only when none was supplied. This keeps the create-time default as a single-responsibility unit on the entity's persistence lifecycle, so a supplied date is preserved and updates are unaffected.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added `registration_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql).\n\nMapStruct maps the same-named `registrationDate` property automatically in both directions, so no mapper or controller changes were needed \u2014 the create flow, telephone/email normalization, and update path stay as they were.",
